Task: emit-input-required-tests + emit-input-required-impl (plan agui_hitl_interrupts_a1f3c2d8, phase P3)

Why: spec FR1. This is the payload of the track — ADK v2.3.0 emits a
workflow input request as a synthetic adk_request_input FunctionCall plus
a typed session.Event.RequestedInput, and the launcher was treating it as
an ordinary tool call.

Changes:
- agui/internal/stream/processor.go: buildInputRequestInterrupt,
  inputRequestFrom, schemaFromArg; adk_request_input registered in
  interruptCallHandlers; Processor.InterruptReasonClassifier field; the
  TODO(non-tool-interrupts) comment deleted.
- agui/stream.go: classifier wired from AGUIConfig into the Processor.
- agui/interrupt_input_test.go (new): 9 tests covering the full interrupt
  shape, boolean schema to confirmation, omitted schema, args fallback,
  typed field winning over args, host classifier override, the three
  schema arg forms plus two rejected ones, and a bare call with nil args.

Design notes:
- metadata.adk.callName is set here but deliberately NOT on tool
  confirmations, whose wire must stay byte identical (acceptance
  criterion 6). interrupt.Record.CallName already defaults to
  toolconfirmation.FunctionCallName when absent.
- schemaFromArg re-types a decoded schema map back into
  *jsonschema.Schema instead of using the map directly. Costs a marshal
  round trip, buys a consistent contract for the host classifier, which
  receives session.RequestInput and would otherwise see a nil schema on
  the round-tripped path.
- ToolCallID left empty and no tool lifecycle emitted; verified by test
  rather than left implicit.

Findings worth carrying forward:
- Coverage for this code needs -coverpkg=./agui/... because the tests
  live in the parent agui package while the code is in internal/stream.
  A plain per-package run reports 0%.
- jsonschema.Schema rejects {"type": 5} at unmarshal with 'invalid value
  for type', which is what exercises the malformed-schema path.

Verification: all pre-existing tests including the tool_call wire
baseline pass unchanged. buildInputRequestInterrupt, inputRequestFrom and
schemaFromArg all at 100%. go fmt, go vet, CI=true go test ./... clean.
